# TEMPLATE for the maintenance supervisor / Ollama health monitor environment on the Oracle host (names and NON-secret placeholders only).
# Intended service: Oracle Cloud Email Delivery. Confirm every value in YOUR OCI console before use; nothing here is a credential.
#
#   1. Console -> Developer Services -> Email Delivery: create an Approved Sender (the exact From address) and complete verification.
#      Configure SPF (and DKIM) for the sender domain as the console instructs, or mail may be rejected or spam-foldered.
#   2. Create SMTP credentials for the IAM user that owns the email resource; the console shows the SMTP username and the one-time password.
#      Store the password ONLY in a root-owned file outside the repository (mode 600), referenced below. Never put it in this file, Git, logs or chat.
#   3. Use the SMTP endpoint shown in the console for your region (pattern: smtp.email.<region>.oci.oraclecloud.com), STARTTLS on port 587.
#
SMTP_HOST=smtp.email.REGION.oci.oraclecloud.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_SECURITY=starttls
SMTP_USER=REPLACE_WITH_SMTP_USERNAME_FROM_THE_CONSOLE
SMTP_PASSWORD_FILE=/etc/azee/secrets/smtp_password
ALERT_MAIL_FROM=REPLACE_WITH_THE_APPROVED_SENDER
ALERT_MAIL_TO=REPLACE_WITH_ADMIN_RECIPIENT_1,REPLACE_WITH_ADMIN_RECIPIENT_2
ALERT_COMMAND=node /opt/azee/scripts/staging/alert-smtp.mjs
# Validate WITHOUT sending:   node scripts/staging/alert-smtp.mjs --check      (prints non-secret facts; exit 3 until fully configured)
